Second prod run (2026-09-04): 315 scored of 364, 38 disagreements, 15 of
them false. All Black Desert, all reuse_existing, all "legacy passed the
sellability gate but the replay skips". The rows recorded internalSales 0;
SaleSignal held 13 sales at $1.75; demandAllocation with 13 sales gives
demand 37 and passes, with 0 it gives 3.7 and skips. The live shadow lane,
reading SaleSignal, agreed with legacy on every one of those decisions. A
disagreement blocks promotion, so this alone would have kept the lane off
Black Desert for a reason that was not real.

Two causes, one disease — the doc's §5.1 again:

  * salesInputsFor short-circuited on a recorded internalSales of 0 and
    returned exact without consulting SaleSignal at all.
  * legacy record() never writes internalSales on the reuse_existing path
    (nor skip_host_offline), so on those rows the field is the schema default
    or a leftover from an earlier decision on the same (game, campaignId) row.
    targetAccounts has the same problem, worse: it is written ONLY on
    farm/probe, and check (c) compared against it on every path — a stale
    target on a reuse row would produce a false "tier target differs".

The row's fields are no longer inputs. Sales always come from SaleSignal
through the window-stability check; the recorded count is used only as an
integrity cross-check, and only on paths that write it
(classes.recordsInternalSales). The tier-target check runs only on paths
that write targetAccounts (classes.recordsTargetAccounts). A recorded zero
on a writing path remains exact whatever the window did since — the
legitimate half of the old shortcut.

The honest cost: a reuse_existing row whose sales window has moved since the
decision is now unreplayable rather than scored, because on that path not
even the count at T is recorded. An unscored row over a false disagreement.
The doc's §9.1 (internalSalesForGame with asOf) is what would recover them.

Every row now carries salesBasis (window_unchanged | recorded_zero) and
salesCount; every disagreement carries a kind (legacy_passed_replay_skips,
legacy_skipped_replay_wants, tier_target, probe_not_reproduced). summarise
adds disagreementKinds and the CLI prints the breakdown by kind and by legacy
decision, so the remaining 23 disagreements can be triaged from the JSON on
the re-run rather than argued about.

Seven new tests, the pinned one being the Black Desert row itself: sales
taken from SaleSignal, salesCount 13, gate passes, agree; the same row with
one sale landed since is unreplayable, never disagree. Suite 672/677, same 5
pre-existing orphan failures. No change to autoFarmer.js or autoLister.js.
